# Sweep-Picked Arpeggios (repertoire plan: st-arpeggio-sweep). An original 8-bar study around
# the 12th fret. Sweep picking: one pick stroke per direction, the pick falling through the
# strings in one motion, down from the lowest string of the shape to string 1, up on the way back.
# Shapes:
#   Am on three strings: string 3 fret 14 (A, finger 3), string 2 fret 13 (C, finger 2),
#   string 1 fret 12 (E, finger 1).
#   C on three strings: string 3 fret 12 (G, finger 1), string 2 fret 13 (C, finger 2),
#   string 1 fret 12 (E, finger 1 again: roll it from string 3 to string 1).
#   Am on five strings: string 5 fret 12 (A, finger 1), string 4 fret 14 (E, finger 3),
#   string 3 fret 14 (A, finger 3 rolled over), string 2 fret 13 (C, finger 2), string 1 fret 12
#   (E, finger 1), then a hammer-on with finger 4 up to string 1 fret 17 (A) and a pull-off back.
# Every note stops as the next one sounds: roll the finger from string to string and lift the
# one behind, so the arpeggio sounds like single notes, never a strummed chord.
# Bars 1-4 in triplets, bars 5-7 in sextuplets (six notes in a beat), bar 8 ends on a held A.
title: Sweep-Picked Arpeggios
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original sweep-picking study
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 8
tags: sweep picking, arpeggios, triplets, sextuplets, a minor, 12th position
tempo: 72
time: 4/4
key: Am

track: Your sweeps
role: lead
